    "reading": {
        "body": "Developer relations hiring in AI is concentrated in a handful of chip and data platform companies, not spread across the industry. Five open roles appear here, and two of them are the same Databricks position posted for San Francisco and Seattle. Lambda, SambaNova, and Databricks are all selling compute or the tooling that runs on it, which is why they need people who can teach developers to use it. The U.S. Air Force Academy posting is the outlier, a faculty role rather than a vendor one, and it is the only listing with a published salary.\n\nThe pattern is narrow. Four of the five roles sit with infrastructure and platform vendors, and three of those are in California. Developer relations is a cost center that only makes sense once a company has a product complex enough to require advocacy, so the listings track the layer of the stack where compute gets sold rather than the layer where models get built. Nothing here speaks to buildings or power directly.\n\nWhat this does not cover is volume. Five postings is a snapshot of one function on one day, not a measure of hiring trend, and the data carries no comparison to prior periods. The source list includes aggregators and a posting-share tracker, but no counts from them appear in these records. Read the companies and the roles, not the totals.",
